The most important missing part is the period axis. Your current page only shows a rolling 60-minute total per line and zone. The original heatmap shows multiple hourly periods, so Python needs one row for every:

```text
Line × Zone × Hour
```

## Recommended model additions

Create these calculated columns or equivalent Power Query columns in `FactRecent`.

```DAX
Period Start =
DATETIME(
    YEAR(FactRecent[DateTime]),
    MONTH(FactRecent[DateTime]),
    DAY(FactRecent[DateTime]),
    HOUR(FactRecent[DateTime]),
    0,
    0
)
```

```DAX
Period Label =
VAR StartTime = FactRecent[Period Start]
RETURN
    FORMAT(StartTime, "h:mm AM/PM")
        & "–"
        & FORMAT(StartTime + TIME(1, 0, 0), "h:mm AM/PM")
```

```DAX
Period Sort =
VALUE(FORMAT(FactRecent[Period Start], "yyyymmddhh"))
```

Then mark:

```text
Period Label → Sort by column → Period Sort
```

Add a numerical order to `DimZone`, such as:

```text
Z1_IN   = 10
Z1_OUT  = 20
Z2A_IN  = 30
Z2A_OUT = 40
Z3_IN   = 50
...
Z6_OUT  = 120
```

## Measures needed

The exact table/column names may differ, but conceptually:

```DAX
Hourly Production =
SUM(FactRecent[Increment])
```

```DAX
Hourly Target =
MAX(DimTarget[HourlyTarget])
```

```DAX
Hourly Attainment =
DIVIDE(
    [Hourly Production],
    [Hourly Target]
)
```

```DAX
Heatmap Status =
VAR Production = [Hourly Production]
VAR Attainment = [Hourly Attainment]
VAR ZeroMinutes = [Consecutive Zero Minutes]
VAR IsStale = [Historian Is Stale]
RETURN
    SWITCH(
        TRUE(),
        IsStale = 1, "STALE",
        ZeroMinutes >= 15, "STOPPED",
        ISBLANK(Production), "NO DATA",
        Attainment >= 0.98, "GREEN",
        Attainment >= 0.90, "YELLOW",
        "RED"
    )
```

The 15-minute stoppage should ideally come from SQL or Power Query rather than complicated DAX. For every minute-level record:

```text
Increment > 0 → running
Increment = 0 → potentially stopped
15 consecutive zero minutes → active zone alert
```

